  "coverage": [
    "Maintained numeric leaves construct plain exact matrices through the existing Core typed constructors for all fourteen supported Bool/index/integer/F32/F64 kinds. Transpose, snapshot sum, matrix binary operations, F64 matrix multiplication and floating unary operations avoid a complete intermediate ValueDataDraft output bank.",
    "The original conservative preflight, cell evaluation order, arithmetic functions, zero seeds, schema/kind checks, equality-sensitive write and atomic publication remain. Unsupported output schemas retain the ordinary draft path. No Core constructor, arithmetic semantics or admission bound was weakened.",
    "Numeric prepared calls retain at most 64 exact geometry bindings with their existing per-binding turn-plan caches. Same identity, schemas, policy, ledger and complete current input/output geometry are checked on every reuse; current payload facts, plans, finite admission and kernel execution remain mandatory.",
    "Every retained slot has independent managed byte/node ownership. Lookup, census and retirement are prepaid. Current coexistence bounds include every binding, index and plan cache plus future binding/plan and ordinary-call workspace. Optional histories retire under pressure; nonnumeric families keep one-slot behavior. Values, pointers, results and permits are never cached.",
    "Four new resident tests compare typed and original draft execution across all fourteen numeric kinds, bit patterns, empty axes, sum seeds, checked overflow, broadcasts, matmul, unary functions, finite ceilings, constrained/complex/string fallbacks, malformed kinds/shapes, old outputs and retry.",
    "Three new original/decoded leaf tests prove actual binding-address and turn-plan reuse over recurring shapes with fresh contents; the 64-slot cap and eviction; foreign identity/account/policy rejection; checked overflow; current-pressure retirement, ordinary-call viability, cleanup and retry."
  ],
